        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/star-wars-zero-company-preview-8.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>There's a funny thing with video game genres in particular: a lot of them are based on just closely tracing the lines of preexisting games, only with a few small mechanical tweaks and a different-enough setting over the top. And few genres are quite as obvious in that regard as the XCOM-alike: a turn-based tactics game based on managing a small squad of permanently-killable allies through a series of close-quarters, grid-based combat encounters, before ducking out to do a bit of RPG-lite housework in some kind of base or mothership metagame. This is Star Wars: Zero Company, a game where you do all of that, but it's Star Wars. And obviously it's completely brilliant.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/star-wars-zero-company-preview-xcom\">Read more</a></p>",
